    "title": "Plymouth County school hosts active shooter drill - NewsBreak",
    "text": "PLYMOUTH COUNTY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — An active shooter drill took place in Plymouth County, Iowa. The training session was underway on Wednesday afternoon. The drill included the county sheriff’s office, Moville Police, Kingsley Police, Fire, and EMS. The active shooter drill occurred at the Kingsley Pierson High School, with the goal for first responders to go through different scenarios that could take place. Story continues below A member of the Plymouth County Sheriff’s Office told KCAU 9 that training in a school helps them in more ways than some people would think. “But by using the school, we’ve got rooms, we’ve got multiple rooms. It gives guys the same knowledge and skill set, as I mean, they can go in and clear a house, or they can clear a school, or they can clear an office building. So it’s a good resource for us. It’s still summertime. They don’t have to worry about interrupting staff and students, and all that. And, you know, it’s good for us and the school as well,” said Chief Deputy Rick Singer from the Plymouth County Sheriff’s Office. Singer said that they train for this scenario every year at different school locations in the county. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
